What:		/sys/class/leds/asus::keyboard/
What:		/sys/class/leds/asus::lightbar/
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Marco Scardovi <scardracs@disroot.org>
Contact:	Denis Benato <denis.benato@linux.dev>
Description:	ASUS Aura keyboard and chassis lightbar Dynamic Lighting nodes.
		Each node accepts its own effect, palette, and direct RGB
		writes. Firmware effects, including static color, are
		committed with Aura 0xb3/0xb5/0xb4 so the controller keeps
		them across reboot. Brightness does not rewrite that packet
		and does not gate the zone: on asus::keyboard it is the
		firmware backlight, and the lightbar has no separate dimmer.
		enabled gates the zone with the power command. The logo
		tracks the keyboard power states. Direct RGB may be backed by HID LampArray
		(Usage Page 0x59) when Aura 0xBC cannot address the lightbar
		independently. The lightbar node is absent when the device
		has no chassis lightbar.

What:		/sys/class/leds/asus::slash/
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Marco Scardovi <scardracs@disroot.org>
Contact:	Denis Benato <denis.benato@linux.dev>
Description:	ASUS ROG Slash LED class device. Exposes brightness together with
		``slash_mode``, ``slash_mode_index``, and ``slash_interval``
		attributes. On Aura keyboards Slash uses feature report 0x5e.
		USB ID 0x193b is shared with AniMe Matrix; the driver claims it
		for Slash only when report size and DMI discrimination select
		Slash rather than AniMe.

What:		/sys/class/leds/asus::anime/
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Marco Scardovi <scardracs@disroot.org>
Contact:	Denis Benato <denis.benato@linux.dev>
Description:	ASUS AniMe Matrix Dynamic Lighting node (USB 0x193b when
		discriminated as AniMe). ``brightness`` is the firmware
		display level (0-3). ``enabled`` maps to display on/off.
		``effect`` selects ``direct`` streaming or a builtin stage
		animation (boot/awake/sleep/shutdown enums). ``direct_buffer``
		accepts one intensity byte per LED; ``led_count`` matches the
		board layout (GA401, GA402, GU604, G635L, G835L). Unknown
		AniMe boards use a GA402-like three-pane layout.
